design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:5:# F_76: Action option — `streaming` or `oneshot` agent mode
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:7:Follow-up on [F_75](F_75_agent_confirm_gate_in_one_shot_cli.md). Add per-action choice: run agent one-shot (current behaviour) or keep a live streaming session that accepts more turns mid-run.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:20:- codex: `codex [--search] exec --json`
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:21:- claude: `claude --print --verbose --output-format stream-json`
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:23:Multi-turn today is **faked**: each turn is a new process, continuity comes from `buildResumeAgentCommand` (`claude --resume <id>` / `codex exec resume --json <id>`) plus transcript replay through `contextInput`. So a conversation = sequence of one-shot processes. One process = one turn = one `assistant` message (`${runId}-assistant`).
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:27:| | one-shot | streaming |
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:29:| claude | `--print --output-format stream-json` | same command + `--input-format stream-json`, stdin stays open, user turns pushed as JSON lines |
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:30:| codex | `exec --json` | **not supported by `exec`** — stdin takes one prompt then closes |
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:32:Claude streaming is a flag plus a stdin writer. Codex streaming needs a different entry point (`codex app-server` JSON-RPC, or `@openai/codex-sdk`), with a different wire protocol than the current JSONL parser. That asymmetry is the bulk of the cost.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:36:New optional action field `mode: 'oneshot' | 'streaming'`, default `oneshot`, agent-actions only (rejected on command actions, same as `trackFileChanges`). Optional per-run override in `runInput`.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:43:- [shared/action_definitions.d.mts](../../shared/action_definitions.d.mts) — `mode?: string` on `RawActionDefinition`, `mode: 'oneshot' | 'streaming'` on `ActionDefinition`.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:44:- [shared/agent_profiles.mjs](../../shared/agent_profiles.mjs) — `STREAMING_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` next to `OUTPUT_COMMAND_ADAPTERS`; claude appends `--input-format stream-json`. Add a `supportsStreaming(profile)` predicate so unknown/custom profiles report false. `buildAgentExecutionCommand` takes the mode.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:52:  - streaming: do **not** `stdin.end()`; write the first turn as a JSON line instead of appending prompt to argv.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:54:  - split **turn end** from **process end**. Today they are the same event. Streaming needs a turn boundary (`result` for claude, `turn.completed` for codex) that resolves the current turn while the process stays alive.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:55:  - `${runId}-assistant` message id assumes one assistant message per run — needs per-turn ids in streaming.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:56:  - `runningConversationIds` guard, conversation persistence, and `onComplete` all hang off `handleClose`; each needs a streaming-aware trigger.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:57:  - lifetime: an idle streaming process must be reaped (idle timeout, or app shutdown via existing `stopAll`).
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:64:- [action_definition_fields.tsx](../../app/src/components/actions/action_definition_fields.tsx) — mode control in the agent-only block beside "Auto commit"; disable/warn when the selected agent profile does not support streaming.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:73:- **Codex has no streaming `exec`.** Without app-server/SDK work, `streaming` is claude-only.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:75:- Persistence currently assumes terminal state at process close; streaming needs incremental persistence or the transcript is lost on crash.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:76:- Codex CLI surface churns — verify `app-server` flags before committing to it.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:80:1. Field + validation + UI, `streaming` accepted but only claude offers it; unsupported profile falls back to `oneshot` with a visible warning.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:81:2. Claude streaming in `agent_runner_service` (stdin writer, turn boundary, per-turn message ids).
design\releases\0_0_3\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:82:3. Codex streaming via `codex app-server` or `@openai/codex-sdk`, as a second protocol adapter.
